From: Koral Ilgun <koral.ilgun@smartrg.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:18:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: skip the first FT key installation on mac80211

wpa_ft_install_ptk() configures the PTK when the FT request arrives,
and again after the association. A driver that tracks the full client
state accepts a pairwise key only for an associated STA, so the first
attempt has two results there, and both are wrong:

- The STA entry is new and not associated. The driver rejects the key,
  and the AP logs "nl80211: kernel reports: key addition failed" at
  error level for each FT over the air.
- With FT over the DS, the AP can still hold an associated entry from
  an earlier association of the STA. The driver accepts the key for
  that entry. add_associated_sta() then replaces the entry for the
  reassociation, and the second attempt gives the same TK to the new
  entry, with a packet number that starts again.

Leave the configuration to the call after the association for such a
driver.
---
 src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c |   21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
@@ -2900,9 +2900,28 @@ void wpa_ft_install_ptk(struct wpa_state
 		return;
 	}
 
-	if (!retry)
+	if (!retry) {
+		u64 drv_flags = 0, drv_flags2 = 0;
+
 		wpa_auth_add_sta_ft(sm->wpa_auth, sm->addr);
 
+		/*
+		 * A driver that tracks the full client state takes a pairwise
+		 * key only for an associated STA. The entry of this exchange
+		 * becomes associated with the Reassociation Request frame. An
+		 * entry that is associated now is from an earlier association
+		 * and gets replaced then, and the same TK must not go to both
+		 * entries. So leave the configuration to the call after the
+		 * association.
+		 */
+		if (sm->wpa_auth->cb->get_drv_flags &&
+		    sm->wpa_auth->cb->get_drv_flags(sm->wpa_auth->cb_ctx,
+						    &drv_flags,
+						    &drv_flags2) == 0 &&
+		    FULL_AP_CLIENT_STATE_SUPP(drv_flags))
+			return;
+	}
+
 	/* FIX: add STA entry to kernel/driver here? The set_key will fail
 	 * most likely without this.. At the moment, STA entry is added only
 	 * after association has been completed. This function will be called
